<title>USA: Value-picker Mark Boyar likes Lehman - Barron's.</title>
<headline>Value-picker Mark Boyar likes Lehman - Barron's.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Value stock investor Mark Boyar cited brokerages, publishers and retailers among his favorite current stock picks, in the March 10 issue of Barron's.</p>
<p>Boyar said he likes Lehman Bros, predicting consolidation in the brokerage industry. He was quoted in Barron's as saying the stock could go over 40.</p>
<p>But if the market craters and the stock declines, the head of Mark Boyar &amp; Co of New York said he'll certainly buy more of it, the story said. Lehman was up 1/8 at 33-1/2 at the close of trading Friday.</p>
<p>Boyar also told Barron's he's staying on Salomon Inc because it could sell as high as 70 over the next 12 to 24 months. Salomon was up 1/4 at 58 at the close of trade Friday.</p>
<p>Boyar's picks include Limited Inc, Dow Jones &amp; Co, Quaker Oats Co, Playboy Enterprises Inc, Toys R Us Inc and Spiegel Inc.</p>
